Statement by the United States Mission to the United Nations on U.S. Nomination of Seven Vessels for Designation by the UN 1718 Committee for DPRK Sanctions Evasion
UNITED STATES MISSION TO THE UNITED NATIONS
Office of Press and Public Diplomacy
FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE
Statement by the United States Mission to the United Nations on U.S. Nomination of Seven Vessels for Designation by the UN 1718 Committee for DPRK Sanctions Evasion
The United States remains committed to the complete denuclearization of North Korea and the rigorous implementation of UN Security Council sanctions on the DPRK. Robust implementation of these sanctions is essential to countering the threat the DPRK’s unlawful weapons programs pose to international peace and security.
Consistent with this commitment, the United States recently nominated seven vessels to the UN 1718 Committee for deflagging and a port entry ban, pursuant to UN Security Council Resolution (UNSCR) 2321.
Between December 2025 and April 2026, these vessels transported DPRK-origin coal or iron ore in violation of UNSCR 2371. Several used deceptive tactics, including AIS manipulation and identity spoofing, to evade detection. This activity supports the DPRK’s unlawful nuclear and ballistic missile programs and meets the criteria for designation under UNSCR 2321.
The nomination builds on the Open Source Centre’s April 2026 briefing to the UN Security Council, which exposed the scale of DPRK maritime sanctions evasion through vessel imagery and voyage analysis. The United States and its partners welcomed that briefing in a May 2026 joint statement urging swift Committee action on the vessels identified and on seven additional vessels nominated in December 2025.
The United States has requested consideration of this nomination under the standard five-day no-objection procedure and calls on all Committee members to act swiftly—both on this nomination and the pending December 2025 designations—to uphold the credibility of UN sanctions and hold accountable those funding the DPRK’s unlawful weapons programs.
The seven vessels nominated this month are:
OSTROV ANTSIFEROVA (IMO 9178070)
EVERSUN (IMO 8356962)
SHUN FA (IMO 1151375)
PEACEFUL 8 (IMO 1039424)
DREAM WAVE (IMO 8693073)
ORION (IMO 9638953)
FU RUN DA 1 (IMO 1099814)
The seven vessels nominated in December 2025 are:
FLYFREE (IMO 1092684)
CASIO (IMO 9125786)
MARS (IMO 1077402)
CARTIER (IMO 1091898)
SOPHIA (aka PRADA) (1079345)
ARMANI (IMO 1078561)
YI LI 1 (IMO 1059149)
