Ambassador Dan Negrea
Representative of the United States to the UN Economic and Social Council
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Ms. Gotoh and Mr. Ratwatte.
Russia’s ballistic missile and drone strikes between July 18 and 19 reportedly killed several people and injured dozens more. One of those missiles struck a civilian grain ship in the Black Sea, killing 10 crew members from India and Syria.
Those casualties, and countless other deaths, could have been avoided, had Russia answered President Trump’s call to negotiate an end to this war.
As we have said before, there is no military solution to this war. Both Ukraine and Russia must return to the negotiating table.
Far too much blood has been spilled. The world is paying a heavy price because of this war. It must end.
The United States renews its call for an immediate ceasefire and for Russia and Ukraine to negotiate in good faith a durable resolution of this war.
The United States remains prepared to play a constructive role to achieve that outcome and to facilitate talks between Moscow and Kyiv. Our commitment to peace in Ukraine is unwavering.
Finally, I must point out that there is a member of this Council that will feign moral outrage and pretend to lecture the rest of us about every topic, whether it’s about the very conflict we’re discussing yet again today, or even those unrelated to international peace and security, like human rights. That is why we walked out during France’s intervention.
This disingenuous grandstanding is tiresome, but we have tolerated it out of a sense of camaraderie and mutual respect as P5 members.
We have stood by this member state through every conflict in which their freedoms have been imperiled. And today, I remind them that it is the United States that remains the beacon of liberty for the world.
As such, we will not be affording them the benefit of listening to their politicized drivel until they renounce their condescending and disrespectful rhetoric and behave in a manner commensurate with their seat on this Council.
I thank you.
