Press Release: Ambassador Mike Waltz Sees Progress from Gang Suppression Force in Haiti Visit
The below is attributable to a U.S. Mission to the United Nations spokesperson:
With the newly deployed Gang Suppression Force (GSF) Haiti’s future is a step in the right direction. With its offensive mandate, Haiti will be more secure, noted U.S. Ambassador Mike Waltz after meeting with senior government officials and regional partners during a recent trip to Haiti.
The U.S. Representative to the United Nations traveled to Haiti to assess the GSF’s progress. The GSF is a key part of the monumental multinational effort to address the security concerns within Haiti. Ambassador Waltz focused on ensuring these efforts yield results as the UN Security Council seeks to renew the GSF’s mandate in September.
This trip reflects President Trump’s commitment to tackling the surge of transnational crime in the region, and in turn, his dedication to the peace and security of the Western Hemisphere.
Follow Ambassador Waltz’s travels on X at @USAmbUN and @USUN.
